<rml>
<head>
    <title>Dialog</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="look.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="dialog.rcss"/>
    <style>
        /* Over a remade screen: what it belongs to alone above the sentence when it has no title; the keys under it. */
        #dialog .titlebar.bare { border-bottom-width: 0; padding-bottom: 0; margin-bottom: 4dp; }
        #dialog .hints { margin-top: 8dp; }
        /* A message's own lines kept (the user's, 26 Nov): 1998's run its parts a line each (REFIT ALL's question: the
           parts with no spare between its words), and the port's add a line to theirs (the room's game data). */
        #dialog #say { white-space: pre-line; }
    </style>
</head>
<!-- Port-only (SPEC-menus.md's stage 3, "When something goes wrong"): a message or question over a remade screen: what
     it belongs to in cyan, its title when it has one, one short sentence under it; the way back at the left and the
     answer at the right (none while a job runs with no way out). -->
<body class="window-body">
    <div class="veil"></div>
    <div class="window-place">
        <div class="dialog panel glass" id="dialog">
            <div class="titlebar" id="titlebar"><div class="eyebrow" id="eyebrow"></div><div class="heading caps" id="heading"></div></div>
            <div class="say" id="say"></div>
            <div class="foot row" id="foot">
                <div class="grow"></div>
                <div class="button" id="other" data-hint="Cancel"></div>
                <div class="button main" id="main" data-hint="OK" data-first></div>
            </div>
            <div class="hints row"><div class="mouse-hints grow"></div><div class="keys"></div></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
